# Pages were being cached for ten minutes, so pressing refresh could hand
# back the version from before a change -- which wasted a good deal of
# everyone's time. no-cache does not stop the browser keeping a copy; it
# makes it ask first, and an unchanged file comes back as a 304.
#
# A rule for /assets/* was tried alongside this one and both applied, which
# produced "no-cache, public, max-age=31536000, immutable" on every asset.
# Scripts and stylesheets already carry a content hash in their URL, so a
# revalidation on them is cheap and the long cache was not worth a
# self-contradicting header.
#
# What a browser is told about handling the site, on every page.
#   - only ever over https, for a year
#   - a file is the type it says it is
#   - no other site may put these pages inside a frame of its own
#     (the Jass table is framed by this site, which SAMEORIGIN allows)
#   - another site is told which site a visitor came from, not which page
#   - the pages ask for no camera, microphone or location
# There is no Content-Security-Policy. The pages carry inline styles and
# scripts, and Clerk, Turnstile and Google Fonts each load from their own
# addresses; a policy written without testing every screen against it
# would break the admin before it stopped anything.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
